  @tag_name "X" <> "XX"

  @moduledoc """
  Flags an `#{@tag_name}` tag left in a comment.

  Credo ships `TagTODO` and `TagFIXME` but no equivalent for the rest of the
  tag vocabulary this project uses. See `.claude/10-comment-tags.md` for the
  full set and which of them block a build.

  `#{@tag_name}` marks code the author already believes is wrong — not work
  deferred (`TODO`) and not a defect being tracked (`BUG`), but a passage
  flagged as suspect at the moment it was written. It blocks for the same
  reason it is purple in the editor: it is the tag people leave when they are
  least sure, which makes it the one least safe to ship unread.
  """

  use Credo.Check,
    base_priority: :high,
    category: :design,
    exit_status: 2,
    param_defaults: [include_doc: true],
    explanations: [
      check: @moduledoc,
